WEBVTT

1
00:00:15.152 --> 00:00:17.252
spun around when he heard Daisy scream.

2
00:00:18.313 --> 00:00:20.253
He saw her throw a towel onto the ground.

3
00:00:21.293 --> 00:00:23.774
Tiny black insects were crawling up her arms!

4
00:00:24.954 --> 00:00:26.855
She raced toward the pool and jumped in.

5
00:00:27.915 --> 00:00:29.996
A second later she came up from underwater.

6
00:00:31.996 --> 00:00:32.736
"Whew!" Daisy said.

7
00:00:32.756 --> 00:00:36.318
"There was a swarm of ants on my towel!

8
00:00:37.399 --> 00:00:40.381
Luckily I rinsed them off before they could bite me."

9
00:00:41.802 --> 00:00:44.563
Henry hurried over to look at the towel Daisy had dropped.

10
00:00:45.704 --> 00:00:48.445
Sure enough, dozens of ants were crawling all over it!

11
00:00:48.465 --> 00:00:50.186
"That's weird."

12
00:00:51.107 --> 00:00:52.808
Cole looked over Henry's shoulder.

13
00:00:52.828 --> 00:00:55.029
"How did those ants get there?"

14
00:00:56.130 --> 00:00:57.931
Henry was wondering the same thing.

15
00:00:58.951 --> 00:01:02.197
He shook off the ants, and then took a closer look at the towel.

16
00:01:03.558 --> 00:01:06.119
It was white, but there was a purple stain on it.

17
00:01:07.160 --> 00:01:10.662
When he sniffed the stain, it smelled sweet, like grape juice.

18
00:01:11.823 --> 00:01:12.363
"What is it?"

19
00:01:12.743 --> 00:01:13.503
Maggie asked.

20
00:01:13.523 --> 00:01:18.686
"Daisy must have spilled her sports drink on her towel," Henry said.

21
00:01:18.706 --> 00:01:21.128
"Ants love sweet stuff."

22
00:01:23.249 --> 00:01:26.051
He went over to where Daisy was talking to Coach Phillips.

23
00:01:27.251 --> 00:01:28.392
Henry showed them the stain.

24
00:01:29.356 --> 00:01:31.617
"Did you spill something on your towel earlier?"

25
00:01:31.957 --> 00:01:32.837
he asked Daisy.

26
00:01:32.857 --> 00:01:36.139
"It's not my towel," Daisy said.

27
00:01:36.159 --> 00:01:40.220
"I forgot mine, so I borrowed that one from Tiny."

28
00:01:40.240 --> 00:01:42.721
"Let me see that, Henry."

29
00:01:43.722 --> 00:01:46.423
Coach Phillips looked at the towel with an anxious frown.

30
00:01:46.443 --> 00:01:50.364
"I hope someone didn't spill their drink in the locker room.

31
00:01:51.345 --> 00:01:52.585
There will be ants everywhere!

32
00:01:53.646 --> 00:01:54.466
I'd better go check."

33
00:01:54.486 --> 00:02:00.529
"I have an extra towel in the office," Lauren told Daisy.

34
00:02:00.549 --> 00:02:02.871
"We'll be right back, everyone."

35
00:02:05.113 --> 00:02:08.495
Coach Phillips, Lauren, and Daisy headed toward the pool building.

36
00:02:08.515 --> 00:02:12.098
"Do you think the ants are connected to the frog prank?"

37
00:02:12.498 --> 00:02:13.479
Maggie asked Henry.

38
00:02:13.499 --> 00:02:16.662
"I'm not sure," Henry said.

39
00:02:16.682 --> 00:02:19.844
"Let's go ask Tiny about his towel."

40
00:02:22.807 --> 00:02:24.808
Henry and Maggie walked over to Tiny.

41
00:02:24.828 --> 00:02:29.172
"Did you know there was grape drink on that towel you loaned to Daisy?"

42
00:02:29.504 --> 00:02:30.305
Maggie demanded.

43
00:02:31.346 --> 00:02:32.326
Tiny shook his head.

44
00:02:32.346 --> 00:02:36.429
"That towel was clean when I put it in my locker this morning.

45
00:02:37.730 --> 00:02:41.613
Maybe Tommy accidentally dragged it in something when he took it out of my locker."

46
00:02:42.794 --> 00:02:45.856
"You mean Tommy was the one who brought the towel to Daisy?"

47
00:02:46.197 --> 00:02:46.997
Henry asked.

48
00:02:48.298 --> 00:02:49.679
"Why didn't you get it yourself?"

49
00:02:50.980 --> 00:02:55.904
"I was busy stretching, so John said he'd ask Tommy to get it," Tiny said.

50
00:02:56.972 --> 00:02:59.634
"But I still feel terrible about what happened."

51
00:03:04.697 --> 00:03:10.521
Cole isn't the only swimmer that Tommy wanted out of tryouts," Henry murmured to Maggie as they walked

52
00:03:10.581 --> 00:03:17.426
away. "Maybe Tommy is trying to chase away all of his competition, including Daisy!"

53
00:03:17.446 --> 00:03:21.909
"That's the only way he could ever make the team," Maggie said.

54
00:03:21.929 --> 00:03:24.150
"Let's go question him!"

55
00:03:25.311 --> 00:03:26.552
She raced toward Tommy.

56
00:03:27.592 --> 00:03:29.273
"Why did you give Daisy that towel?"

57
00:03:30.654 --> 00:03:31.955
Tommy looked confused.

58
00:03:31.975 --> 00:03:37.139
"Because Daisy forgot hers, and Tiny had an extra one," he said.

59
00:03:37.159 --> 00:03:39.941
"How did that grape stuff get on there?"

60
00:03:40.321 --> 00:03:41.062
Maggie demanded.

61
00:03:41.082 --> 00:03:43.123
"And all those ants?"

62
00:03:44.304 --> 00:03:45.925
"I don't know," Tommy said.

63
00:03:47.266 --> 00:03:50.068
Henry couldn't tell if Tommy was lying or telling the truth.

64
00:03:51.269 --> 00:03:55.332
Either way Henry was afraid that Maggie's questions might make him mad.

65
00:03:56.384 --> 00:03:57.865
He quickly changed the subject.

66
00:03:57.885 --> 00:04:00.526
"Hey, Tommy," he said.

67
00:04:00.546 --> 00:04:03.687
"Why did you decide to try out for the swim team?"

68
00:04:05.148 --> 00:04:08.469
"My parents wanted me to get some exercise this summer," Tommy said.

69
00:04:08.489 --> 00:04:11.390
"I thought it would be fun to swim with my brother.

70
00:04:12.291 --> 00:04:13.911
Too bad I stink at swimming!"

71
00:04:14.672 --> 00:04:15.272
He laughed.

72
00:04:16.292 --> 00:04:19.393
Just then John came over to give him some swimming tips.

73
00:04:20.574 --> 00:04:22.235
Henry and Maggie wandered away.

74
00:04:22.255 --> 00:04:25.476
"Do you think Tommy's telling the truth?"

75
00:04:25.928 --> 00:04:26.709
Maggie asked.

76
00:04:27.870 --> 00:04:29.831
"I'm not sure," Henry said.

77
00:04:29.851 --> 00:04:32.373
"Let's go see what Cole thinks."

78
00:04:33.534 --> 00:04:35.075
Cole was checking on the frogs.

79
00:04:35.095 --> 00:04:37.476
"Did you solve the mystery yet?"

80
00:04:37.877 --> 00:04:38.457
he asked.

81
00:04:39.578 --> 00:04:42.500
"Not yet," Henry said, keeping his voice low.

82
00:04:42.520 --> 00:04:45.162
"But we have a couple of suspects.

83
00:04:46.303 --> 00:04:47.544
One of them is Tommy Miller."

84
00:04:47.564 --> 00:04:53.108
"We think he might be trying to get you kicked out of tryouts," added Maggie.

85
00:04:54.220 --> 00:04:56.421
"That way he'll have a better chance to make the team."

86
00:04:56.441 --> 00:04:59.123
"Tommy?" Cole shook his head.

87
00:04:59.143 --> 00:05:00.524
"No way.

88
00:05:00.564 --> 00:05:01.544
He's a nice kid.

89
00:05:02.565 --> 00:05:04.946
Plus he's not competitive like his older brother.

90
00:05:05.887 --> 00:05:07.748
Tommy doesn't care if he makes the team or not."

91
00:05:09.088 --> 00:05:10.929
Just then Kyle marched over.

92
00:05:11.990 --> 00:05:14.011
He was two years older than Henry and Cole.

93
00:05:14.031 --> 00:05:19.394
"You should go home and take your frogs with you, Cole," Kyle said loudly.

94
00:05:19.414 --> 00:05:22.636
"Fifth-grade nerds don't belong here!

95
00:05:23.636 --> 00:05:26.098
You should have tried out for the junior swim team."

96
00:05:26.118 --> 00:05:30.420
"I'll be in sixth grade in the fall," Cole told him.

97
00:05:30.440 --> 00:05:33.262
"That means I can try out for either team."

98
00:05:34.303 --> 00:05:38.445
Kyle took a sip of the purple sports drink he was holding, and then smirked.

99
00:05:39.646 --> 00:05:40.247
"Oh yeah?"

100
00:05:40.587 --> 00:05:41.027
he said.

101
00:05:41.047 --> 00:05:44.649
"I just heard Coach Phillips talking to Lauren.

102
00:05:45.730 --> 00:05:48.552
She's trying to talk him into kicking you out of tryouts!"
